{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY**\n\n1. **A diagnostic retry can still decide whether the scored test completes.** In a $0 replay, all 36 first attempts were recorded and the counts stayed at 9 joint pairs and 3 separate pairs. The verdict was `PASS` when the last diagnostic retry returned and `INCOMPLETE` when it failed in transport or was skipped. Send all first attempts before spending on diagnostic retries, and determine scoring completeness from the first attempts. Keep retry failures in the diagnostic record. [paid_gate.py:181](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:181) · [paid_gate.py:687](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:687)\n\n2. **A format failure can still make the run unreadable.** I replayed a provider refusal with `content: null`. Packet generation crashed after creating the Markdown files and before saving the key. A second invocation then failed because the files already existed. A separate replay showed that the 20,000-character journal cut dropped a cited passage ID from a long malformed answer. Preserve the full returned text or refusal in the harness, handle null content, and render both files successfully before publishing the packet bundle. [paid_gate.py:169](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:169) · [paid_gate.py:551](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:551) · [paid_gate.py:600](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:600)"}}
